{"id": "x21", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C3", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Hasil tes urine Budi menunjukkan adanya darah. Pemeriksaan lanjutan yang paling tepat adalah ...", "a": "Memeriksakan ginjal dan saluran kemih ke dokter", "s": ["Mengurangi minum air", "Menambah makanan asin", "Menunggu sembuh sendiri"], "e": "Darah dalam urine perlu diperiksa dokter karena bisa disebabkan infeksi, batu, atau kerusakan ginjal."},
{"id": "x22", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Di cuaca panas orang lebih banyak berkeringat daripada buang air kecil. Penjelasan yang tepat adalah ...", "a": "Air tubuh banyak keluar lewat kulit untuk mendinginkan tubuh", "s": ["Ginjal berhenti bekerja", "Paru-paru membuang air", "Hati membuat keringat"], "e": "Di cuaca panas, keringat membantu mendinginkan tubuh sehingga lebih banyak air keluar lewat kulit dan urine menjadi lebih sedikit."},
{"id": "x23", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C3", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Seseorang nyeri hebat di pinggang dan urinenya sedikit berdarah setelah jarang minum. Dugaan penyebabnya adalah ...", "a": "Batu ginjal", "s": ["Hepatitis", "Asma", "Biang keringat"], "e": "Nyeri pinggang dengan urine berdarah setelah jarang minum khas batu ginjal yang melukai saluran kemih."},
{"id": "x24", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Perbedaan hepatitis dan sirosis hati adalah ...", "a": "Hepatitis berupa peradangan hati, sirosis berupa jaringan hati rusak dan mengeras", "s": ["Hepatitis menyerang ginjal, sirosis menyerang paru-paru", "Hepatitis akibat batu, sirosis akibat keringat", "Keduanya sama persis"], "e": "Hepatitis adalah peradangan hati, sedangkan sirosis adalah kerusakan permanen jaringan hati yang mengeras."},
{"id": "x25", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C3", "bhs": "EN", "q": "A student notices her urine is pale and plentiful after drinking lots of water. What does this show?", "a": "The kidneys excreted the excess water", "s": ["The liver stopped working", "The lungs removed urea", "The skin stopped sweating"], "e": "Extra water is not reabsorbed, so the kidneys excrete it as pale, plentiful urine."},
{"id": "x26", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "EN", "q": "Why do athletes lose body salts when they sweat heavily?", "a": "Sweat contains salts (NaCl) as well as water", "s": ["Sweat is pure water", "Salt is made in the lungs", "Salt comes from bile"], "e": "Sweat contains salts (NaCl) along with water, so heavy sweating loses salts too."},
{"id": "x27", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C3", "bhs": "EN", "q": "Which test result would suggest kidney damage?", "a": "Protein in the urine", "s": ["Water in the urine", "Salt in the urine", "Urea in the urine"], "e": "Protein in the urine suggests the glomerulus is damaged and lets protein leak through."},
{"id": "x28", "no": 0, "kat": "M", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "EN", "q": "Why do blood ammonia levels rise in liver cirrhosis?", "a": "The liver cannot convert ammonia into urea", "s": ["The kidneys make extra ammonia", "The lungs absorb ammonia", "Sweat contains ammonia"], "e": "A damaged liver cannot turn toxic ammonia into urea, so ammonia builds up in the blood."},
{"id": "x29", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Kadar glukosa darah pasien normal, tetapi urinenya mengandung glukosa. Analisis yang paling tepat adalah ...", "a": "Tubulus proksimal rusak sehingga glukosa tidak diserap kembali", "s": ["Glomerulus tidak menyaring glukosa", "Hati mengubah glukosa menjadi urea", "Kulit mengeluarkan glukosa"], "e": "Glukosa darah normal berarti penyaringan wajar; glukosa di urine menunjukkan reabsorpsi di tubulus proksimal gagal."},
{"id": "x30", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C5", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Seseorang banyak makan protein tetapi sedikit minum. Dampak jangka panjang yang paling mungkin dan alasannya adalah ...", "a": "Beban ginjal meningkat karena urea hasil pemecahan protein banyak dan perlu dibuang bersama air", "s": ["Hati berhenti membuat empedu", "Paru-paru membuang urea", "Keringat menggantikan fungsi ginjal"], "e": "Pemecahan protein menghasilkan banyak urea yang harus dibuang ginjal bersama air, sehingga kurang minum menambah beban ginjal."},
{"id": "x31", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Pasien A berurine encer dan banyak dengan ADH rendah, pasien B berurine pekat dan sedikit dengan ADH tinggi. Kesimpulan yang tepat adalah ...", "a": "ADH mendorong penyerapan kembali air sehingga urine menjadi pekat", "s": ["ADH menghambat penyerapan air", "ADH menambah penyaringan glukosa", "ADH mengubah amonia menjadi urea"], "e": "ADH meningkatkan reabsorpsi air; ADH rendah menghasilkan urine encer dan banyak, ADH tinggi menghasilkan urine pekat dan sedikit."},
{"id": "x32", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C5", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Siswa merancang kampanye menjaga ginjal. Rancangan yang paling tepat dan beralasan adalah ...", "a": "Minum cukup, tidak menahan buang air kecil, dan kurangi garam karena mencegah batu ginjal dan infeksi", "s": ["Minum sedikit agar jarang ke toilet", "Banyak makan makanan asin agar mineral cukup", "Minum obat pereda nyeri setiap hari"], "e": "Minum cukup, tidak menahan buang air kecil, dan mengurangi garam mencegah batu ginjal serta infeksi saluran kemih."},
{"id": "x33", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Penderita hepatitis mengalami urine cokelat tua dan kulit kuning. Hubungan yang tepat adalah ...", "a": "Bilirubin menumpuk di darah dan sebagian keluar lewat urine", "s": ["Glukosa banyak dikeluarkan", "Protein membasahi urine", "Kulit mengubah urea menjadi empedu"], "e": "Pada hepatitis, hati gagal mengolah bilirubin sehingga menumpuk dan sebagian keluar lewat urine, membuatnya cokelat tua."},
{"id": "x34", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C5", "bhs": "ID", "q": "Urea dibuang lewat urine dan sedikit lewat keringat. Mengapa ginjal tetap organ ekskresi utama untuk urea?", "a": "Ginjal membuang urea jauh lebih banyak dan sekaligus mengatur keseimbangan air serta garam", "s": ["Keringat membuang seluruh urea", "Paru-paru membuang urea", "Hati menyimpan urea selamanya"], "e": "Ginjal membuang urea dalam jumlah jauh lebih besar dibanding keringat dan sekaligus mengatur keseimbangan air serta garam."},
{"id": "x35", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "EN", "q": "Patient X has normal blood glucose, yet glucose appears in the urine. The best analysis is ...", "a": "The proximal tubule is damaged and cannot reabsorb glucose", "s": ["The glomerulus fails to filter glucose", "The liver turns glucose into urea", "The skin removes glucose"], "e": "Normal blood glucose but glucose in the urine means reabsorption in the proximal tubule has failed."},
{"id": "x36", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C5", "bhs": "EN", "q": "A person eats a lot of protein and drinks very little. Which long-term effect and reason is most likely?", "a": "A heavier kidney workload, because more urea must be removed with water", "s": ["The liver stops making bile", "The lungs remove urea", "Sweat replaces the kidneys"], "e": "Protein breakdown makes urea, which the kidneys remove with water; drinking too little increases their workload."},
{"id": "x37", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "EN", "q": "Patient A makes large amounts of dilute urine, patient B makes small amounts of concentrated urine. Which conclusion is correct?", "a": "A has low ADH and B has high ADH", "s": ["A has high ADH and B has low ADH", "Both have normal ADH", "ADH has no role in urine volume"], "e": "Low ADH means less water is reabsorbed, giving dilute urine; high ADH gives concentrated urine."},
{"id": "x38", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C5", "bhs": "EN", "q": "A class designs a poster to protect the liver. Which design is best, and why?", "a": "Avoid alcohol, wash hands, eat clean food, and get vaccinated, because these prevent liver damage and hepatitis", "s": ["Drink a little alcohol every day", "Skip meals to rest the liver", "Take any herbal medicine freely"], "e": "Avoiding alcohol, washing hands, eating clean food, and vaccination protect the liver from damage and hepatitis."},
{"id": "x39", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C4", "bhs": "EN", "q": "A patient has very high blood urea and almost no urine. Which organ has most likely failed?", "a": "Kidney", "s": ["Skin", "Lungs", "Stomach"], "e": "High blood urea and very little urine point to kidney failure, because the kidneys cannot remove urea."},
{"id": "x40", "no": 0, "kat": "H", "lv": "C5", "bhs": "EN", "q": "Evaluate: \"The lungs excrete CO₂, so they do not need protection from smoke.\" The correct judgment is ...", "a": "False, because smoke damages the alveoli and weakens CO₂ excretion", "s": ["True, because CO₂ leaves through the skin", "True, because the liver removes CO₂", "False, because smoke affects only the kidneys"], "e": "Smoke damages alveoli, so lungs exposed to smoke excrete CO₂ less efficiently and need protection."}
